<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ioannis Kapodistrias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1776–1831</span> · Also known as John Capodistria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ioannis Kapodistrias was a Corfiot nobleman who served as a secretary of state of the Septinsular Republic and then as a Russian diplomat and joint foreign minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> from 1816 to 1822. Elected first governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> in 1827, he arrived in 1828 and built a central administration, schools and a currency, the phoenix. His authoritarian rule provoked opposition, and he was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nafplio</a> in 1831 by members of the Mavromichalis family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ioannis-kapodistrias.jpg" alt="Ioannis Kapodistrias" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dionysios Tsokos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kapodistrias2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
